Sourceforge keeps changing its policies and procedures for site
maintenance.  Here are the notes from putting out version 5.1 to be
used in deploying future versions.

# Prerequisites 

## Fully test the release, and ensure that all compiler warnings have
   been silenced (both for Prolog and C code)

## Make sure that all files in XSB/docs/homepage are up to date with
   the correct version number.

## Make sure that the versioning in the manuals is up to date and has
   the new release number.

# Make the zip/gz files

## Make sure that XSB/build/version.sh is up to date with the correct
   release number.

  After fully testing the releaese in your working tree, commit any
  changed files and tag (git tag <name>)

  The run admin/TarRelease.sh <version> /target/path tag

  this will create a zip and gz file.

# Updating the webpage files

# Update the webpage

make whatever changes you need in docs/homepage, and when you are
   done update git.

-- sftp tswift@web.sourceforge.net

   (substitute your name, if anyone else ever makes a release besides
   me.. sigh)

   lcd gives the local directory by the way.
   
   ## Then cd to /home/project-web/xsb/htdocs

   Copy into the various directories any of the .html or other files
   you need.  Eg.

   put index.html
   put changelog.html
   put research.html
   put about.html
   etc.

   Also update the directories
   manual1
   manual2
   
   To fool sourceforge's cache, you may need to append the url with
   ?update=1 

-- There are several other directories that may need to be updated,
   but these are tbe basics

# Updating the download

## Now sftp tswift cd /home/frs/project/xsb and upload the zip/gz
   file(s)

-- Finally, update the news.  Login to sourceforge, under the admin
menu, click news, then submit.  this will bring you to a form where
you can submit the news story.

